The brief has changed. Here is the change, in addition to everything the brief said before:

# Change 3: pause a run

An operator can now pause a run, so that no queued task starts until the run is resumed.

- `pause(run)`: a run that is not paused becomes paused. Refused when it is paused.
- `resume(run)`: a paused run is no longer paused. Refused when it is not paused.
- `taskStarted(run, task)` is refused while the run is paused. Every other command works as before on a paused run.

`run(run)` now also returns `paused`, a boolean, false for a run that was never paused. Pausing does not change the run's status. Everything else is as before.

The host interface is now as follows, and `host.ts` has been updated to match.

```ts
// T5 after change 3, workflow run status with retries, single cancels and pauses: the host interface every arm implements (PT13).

/** The outcome of a command: it took effect, or it was refused and changed nothing. */
export type Outcome = { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string };

export type Status = 'queued' | 'running' | 'evicted' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'cancelled';

export interface RunView {
  status: Status;
  task0: Status;
  task1: Status;
  task2: Status;
  paused: boolean;
}

export interface Host {
  start(run: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskStarted(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskCompleted(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskFailed(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskEvicted(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskRequeued(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskRetried(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  cancel(run: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  cancelTask(run: string, task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  pause(run: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  resume(run: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  /** The run, or null when no run has that id. */
  run(run: string): Promise<RunView | null>;
}

/** The module's default export: a factory of a fresh system, with no runs. */
export type CreateHost = () => Promise<Host>;
